1
00:00:00,350 --> 00:00:01,796
Give hydrogen enough time,

2
00:00:02,046 --> 00:00:04,270
and it starts asking where it came from.

3
00:00:05,170 --> 00:00:07,007
13.8 billion years ago,

4
00:00:07,007 --> 00:00:10,523
the Big Bang made hydrogen, a little helium,

5
00:00:10,823 --> 00:00:12,740
and almost nothing else!

6
00:00:13,640 --> 00:00:15,203
Then gravity went to work.

7
00:00:15,453 --> 00:00:16,655
It squeezed that gas

8
00:00:16,655 --> 00:00:19,000
until the first stars burst into light!

9
00:00:19,900 --> 00:00:23,234
Inside them, hydrogen fused, step by step,

10
00:00:23,234 --> 00:00:24,821
into carbon, oxygen,

11
00:00:25,071 --> 00:00:26,500
the atoms of life.

12
00:00:27,400 --> 00:00:28,586
Those stars died,

13
00:00:28,586 --> 00:00:31,168
and blasted their atoms across space.

14
00:00:31,418 --> 00:00:33,720
New suns formed. Planets. Oceans.

15
00:00:34,620 --> 00:00:35,156
And you?

16
00:00:35,456 --> 00:00:37,131
About 6 of every 10 atoms

17
00:00:37,131 --> 00:00:38,874
in your body are hydrogen,

18
00:00:39,174 --> 00:00:41,720
almost all of it made in the Big Bang.

19
00:00:42,620 --> 00:00:44,207
You are that ancient gas,

20
00:00:44,207 --> 00:00:45,730
looking up at the stars.

21
00:00:46,130 --> 00:00:47,590
Which proves one thing.
